AUDIO: 'pixels. The person looks exactly the same. The shirt is exactly the same. The writing came out perfectly from our reference photo. Yeah, the background looks really good. You can see that it definitely enhanced the quality of the'

[16:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'pixels while maintaining the same look of the animals, stuffed animals, and so on. All right, for the final example, what I\'m going to do here is I\'m going to disable our second image pass to show you guys how to use an edit workflow'

[16:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'with just one reference photo. So, I\'m going to hold down control or command if you\'re on a Mac, drag over these nodes, these four nodes here that are our second image pass. And I\'m going to press control B or command B on my'

[16:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'keyboard and that\'ll bypass all of the nodes that correspond to our second image pass. Now, I\'m going to refine the prompt here and just describe this person somewhere else. All right, so the prompt that I\'m going to be using is'

[17:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'replace the background and relight the photo to match the following environment. A dimly city alleyway with graffiti covering the walls. So, let\'s see what this generation outputs. All right, here\'s the product from that run of the workflow, and you can see'

[17:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that it definitely re-lit the entire image properly, especially the lighting on the person. That\'s what we\'re focusing on the most here. And obviously, with a bit more of a detailed prompt, I could get the graffiti to say'

[17:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'something in particular if I wanted to. And you can really just describe everything that you want, and be as specific as you want in order to get whatever results you\'re really looking for. I actually wanted to do one more example for you guys here. So, I took a'

[17:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'picture of a Louis Vuitton handbag and prompted to place the handbag hanging naturally from the shoulder of the woman between her torso and her relaxed arm. The output that we got, the bag looks perfect. It maintained the exact texture'

[17:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and patterns that you would see on the bag in the reference photo. And it placed it naturally hanging from her shoulder between her torso and her arm just as prompted. You can see that that prompt was very simple and'

[18:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'straightforward, but it still did quite a good job. So, now you guys have a genuine edit workflow. The one idea to walk away with is that references live in the conditioning, not the latent. So, your photos become instructions. Everything else in this build was'

[18:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'plumbing around that one move. If you want to take this further than I did today, you can chain a third reference with another image pass-through if you want to. So, you could put a person, for example, something like a handbag, sunglasses, and outfit in the second,'

[18:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and the background or the setting or environment in the third. So, that\'s pretty much going to wrap up Build With Me episode 4. Thank you guys so much for watching. Please, if you liked it, like the video, subscribe, hop in the'

